<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 30 January, from 1649 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1649 <span class="tih-ago">377 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles I is beheaded in Whitehall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Convicted of treason, Charles I was executed on a scaffold outside the Banqueting House. England became a republic, and the monarchy was not restored until 1660.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1835 <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson survives an assassination attempt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the US Capitol, the house painter Richard Lawrence fired two pistols at Jackson, but both misfired. It was the first known attempt to kill a sitting American president.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1882 <span class="tih-ago">144 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Franklin D. Roosevelt is born at Hyde Park, New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roosevelt led the United States through the Great Depression and most of the Second World War. He is the only president elected four times.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1933 <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler appointed Chancellor of Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Hindenburg made the Nazi leader Chancellor, with conservatives expecting to control him. Within months Hitler had suspended civil liberties and established a one-party dictatorship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet submarine sinks the Wilhelm Gustloff</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Torpedoes from submarine S-13 sank the overcrowded German liner in the Baltic as it evacuated refugees and military personnel. An estimated 9,000 died, the greatest loss of life in a single sinking.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1948 <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mahatma Gandhi is assassinated in New Delhi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hindu nationalist Nathuram Godse shot Gandhi at a prayer meeting at Birla House. The death of the leader of India's non-violent independence struggle was mourned across the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1968 <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tet Offensive begins in South Vietnam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">North Vietnamese and Viet Cong forces attacked towns and bases across South Vietnam during the lunar new year truce. Though repelled, the offensive undermined American confidence in the war.</p></div></li></ol>
